--- body ---
## Problem

Existing tests (erg_test.go, validate_test.go) exercise parser and
validator internals. No tests call the compiled binary end-to-end, so
dispatch errors, --help output, exit codes, and file-writing commands
(close, log, archive) are untested at the integration level.

## Plan

1. Add cli_test.go with a TestMain that builds the binary once into
   t.TempDir(). Use the standard Go pattern: exec.Command(binary, args)
   and assert on stdout, stderr, and exit code.

2. Add testdata fixture directories named after scenarios (check-pass,
   check-dup-id, close-happy, close-already, log-append, etc.).

3. Table-driven subtests covering at minimum:
   - erg validate: pass, fail, directory rejection
   - erg check: pass, duplicate ID, cycle
   - erg close: happy path, already closed, missing ticket
   - erg log: happy path, missing separator
   - erg ready: with and without --json
   - erg version: smoke (exit 0, prints path)
   - erg --help: prints usage
   - erg --help --all: prints all command help
   - unknown command: exit 1

4. No external dependencies. Use os/exec + testdata fixtures only.

## Exit criteria

- `go test ./...` passes with the new integration tests.
- Each command has at least one happy-path and one error-path test.
- Zero new dependencies in go.mod.
